course: dictionary
lesson: 12193
title: Confide: sharing a secret
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To confide means to tell someone a secret or a private worry because you trust them. Context helps here too. «Maya confided in her best friend that she felt scared about the new school.» Who did she tell? A friend. Why? Because she trusted her, and the worry was private.
explain: Look at the clues: secret, private worry and trust all point to the same idea. Try the check: swap in «told» and see if it still makes sense. «Maya told her best friend that she felt scared» works, but confided shows that the worry was private and shared because of trust.
explain: Confide can also mean saying something quietly, as a secret. «Tom confided that he had broken the window by accident.» He said it privately, not in front of the whole class. If someone hurts you, a safe step is to confide in a grown-up you trust.
fact: Confide is a verb. Its forms are confide, confides, confided and confiding.
fact: «Confide in» means to tell someone a secret or private worry because you trust them.
fact: «Confided» is the past tense: «She confided that she was nervous about the test.»
fact: A confidant is a person you trust with your secrets.
fact: Formal use: to confide something to someone means to give it into their care, such as «She confided the keys to her neighbour.»
exercise: «Ella confided in her teacher about the bullying.» What does confided in mean here? | Gave the teacher a present | *Told her teacher a private worry because she trusted her | Forgot about it completely | Shouted the news across the playground
exercise: «Sam confided that he felt lonely since moving house.» What did Sam share? | A plan to move house again | *A private, sad feeling | A new football | A loud joke for the class
exercise: «She needed someone to confide in.» Who would be a good person to confide in if you are worried? | Your pet goldfish, because it will tell everyone | Nobody, so keep it secret forever | *A grown-up you trust | A stranger on the street
test: What does confide mean? | To shout a warning across a room | *To tell a secret or private worry to someone you trust | To hide something under the bed | To write a long letter to a newspaper
test: Which phrase means the same as «confided that»? | *Told privately that | Forgot that | Asked whether | Shouted loudly that
exam: Your friend confides in you about a secret. What is the kindest thing to do? | Ignore them forever | *Keep it private and help them tell a grown-up if they are hurt | Tell the whole class straight away | Laugh and share it online
